<h1 class="text-4xl pb-4 border-b border-dashed border-terminal-dim">Commands Reference</h1>

<p class="text-2xl pt-6 pb-4">
  Every command the player can type, with all synonyms and how the engine parses them.
</p>

<h2 id="parsing" class="doc-section text-3xl pt-6 pb-3 border-b border-terminal-dim">How Commands Are Parsed</h2>

<p class="text-xl pt-4 pb-3">
  The CommandParser breaks player input into three parts:
</p>

<pre class="doc-code text-terminal-green mt-2"><span class="comment">// "use key on door" becomes:</span>
{
  <span class="key">"verb"</span>:     <span class="str">"use"</span>,      <span class="comment">// the action</span>
  <span class="key">"target"</span>:   <span class="str">"key"</span>,      <span class="comment">// first object</span>
  <span class="key">"modifier"</span>: <span class="str">"door"</span>,     <span class="comment">// second object (after preposition)</span>
  <span class="key">"raw"</span>:      <span class="str">"use key on door"</span>
}</pre>

<p class="text-xl pt-3">
  Articles (<code>the</code>, <code>a</code>, <code>an</code>) and prepositions (<code>to</code>, <code>at</code>, <code>on</code>, <code>with</code>, <code>from</code>, <code>of</code>) are stripped during parsing.
</p>

